Text: "Real analysis studies approximation on the ordered field
       $\mathbb{R}$. Its decisive axiom is completeness: bounded nonempty sets
       possess least upper bounds, equivalently Cauchy sequences converge.
       Completeness turns local estimates into existence theorems and explains
       why analogous assertions can fail over $\mathbb{Q}$.

       The chapter proceeds from the real number system to sequences and
       series, then to limits and continuity, differentiation, and Riemann
       integration. Quantifiers are part of the substance. In every limit
       definition, the order and dependence of $\epsilon$, $\delta$, indices,
       and points determine the concept being defined."
Id: "6014cc04-2098-48f7-b489-7d997516d9f0"
